      "explanation": "<p>In protein chemistry, each amino acid is assigned a one-letter code to simplify notation. The matching for the given amino acids to their one-letter codes is as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arginine (A) - R (IV)</li>\n<li>Aspartic Acid (B) - D (I)</li>\n<li>Asparagine (C) - N (II)</li>\n<li>Alanine (D) - A (III)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So, the correct answer is Option C: (A) - IV, (B) - I, (C) - II, (D) - III.</p>\n"
